2. Mandatory ProsenjitOS name for derivative operating systems

If you modify, adapt, fork, or create a derivative work from ProsenjitOS and
distribute it as an operating system, OS distribution, or installable/
bootable OS product, its primary product name must remain exactly
"ProsenjitOS".

You must not rename such a derivative operating system to a different
primary OS/product name, remove "ProsenjitOS" from its primary OS identity,
or distribute it as a separately named replacement operating system.

This condition applies to the name of the distributed OS product. It does
not require every application, package, library, tool, service, theme,
website, organization, or independent project that merely uses a separately
licensed interface or interoperates with ProsenjitOS to be named
"ProsenjitOS".

You may identify your own modifications, edition, build, maintainer, or
organization in a truthful secondary designation, provided the primary OS
name remains "ProsenjitOS" and the designation does not falsely imply
official endorsement, certification, or support by the upstream project.

